          "title": "Single-Threaded Model and Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. One Thread for JS",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "JS runs on ==one main thread==: one **call stack**, one callback at a time",
                "So no ==data races== on plain JS variables",
                "Single-threaded for **JS only**: {blue:libuv}, the {purple:OS kernel} and a {orange:thread pool} do I/O and heavy work"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Mental Model",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Stack",
                    "sub": "runs sync code",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Background",
                    "sub": "libuv, kernel, pool",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Queues",
                    "sub": "finished callbacks",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Event loop",
                    "sub": "push one at a time",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. I/O-bound vs CPU-bound",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "I/O-bound",
                "CPU-bound"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Example",
                  "many sockets, little CPU",
                  "heavy computation"
                ],
                [
                  "Fit",
                  "{green:Good}",
                  "{red:Bad}"
                ],
                [
                  "Why",
                  "waiting happens off-thread",
                  "one slow callback delays every request"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A slow ==callback== makes every other request wait. Node scales on **waiting**, not on computing."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Really single-threaded?** JS yes; libuv and the thread pool work in the background",
                "**10k connections?** Sockets wait in the kernel; ready callbacks run one at a time",
                "**CPU work a problem?** One slow callback blocks the stack, so all requests wait"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
