    {
      "title": "nextTick vs setImmediate vs setTimeout",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "nextTick vs setImmediate vs setTimeout",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Who Runs Where",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "API",
                "Runs in",
                "When"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`process.nextTick`",
                  "nextTick queue",
                  "right after current operation"
                ],
                [
                  "`Promise.then`",
                  "microtask queue",
                  "after nextTick queue drains"
                ],
                [
                  "`setImmediate`",
                  "check phase",
                  "same loop turn"
                ],
                [
                  "`setTimeout(fn, 0)`",
                  "timers phase",
                  "later turn (0 → 1ms)"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Order Proof",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "setTimeout(() => console.log('timeout'), 0);",
                "setImmediate(() => console.log('immediate'));",
                "Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('promise'));",
                "process.nextTick(() => console.log('tick'));",
                "console.log('sync');"
              ],
              "note": "CommonJS file"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "sync",
                "tick",
                "promise",
                "timeout",
                "immediate"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:CommonJS}: sync → ==nextTick== → promise → timeout/immediate",
                "{red:ES module}: ==promise before tick==, the module body runs in a microtask",
                "Main module: timeout vs immediate is ==non-deterministic=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Rules and Traps",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inside an I/O callback, `setImmediate` ==always== fires first",
                "Use it to deterministically run after I/O"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Starvation",
              "text": "Recursive `process.nextTick` never lets the loop advance, so **I/O starves**. Yield with `setImmediate` instead."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Blocking the Event Loop",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Blocking the Event Loop",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What blocking is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Blocking== = one callback runs long **synchronously**",
                "Timers, requests, I/O all {red:wait}: p99 latency spikes for **every client**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Culprits and fixes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Culprit",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`fs.readFileSync`, any `*Sync`",
                  "async API"
                ],
                [
                  "Huge `JSON.parse/stringify`",
                  "chunk or worker"
                ],
                [
                  "ReDoS-prone regex",
                  "safer pattern, worker"
                ],
                [
                  "Big loops",
                  "chunk, `setImmediate`"
                ],
                [
                  "Sync crypto",
                  "async crypto, child process"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "function run(a, i = 0) {",
                "  for (let n = 0; n < 500 && i < a.length; n++) work(a[i++]);",
                "  if (i < a.length) setImmediate(run, a, i);",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "yield between chunks"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Detect it",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`perf_hooks.monitorEventLoopDelay()` samples loop lag",
                "Sustained high ==p99== delay = blocked loop",
                "`--cpu-prof` shows the hot function"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Find the blocker?** Delay histogram, then `--cpu-prof`",
                "**Sync OK at startup?** Runs once before serving; in a handler it stalls every client",
                "**Break a long loop?** Chunks, yield with `setImmediate`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Offload CPU work to a ==worker thread== or child process."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Worker Threads for CPU-Bound Work",
      "role": "outline",
