          "title": "Worker Threads for CPU-Bound Work",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Worker Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Separate thread: own ==V8 isolate==, event loop, memory",
                "Messages are copied by ==structured clone==",
                "==Transfer== an ArrayBuffer: moved, not copied",
                "`SharedArrayBuffer` + `Atomics` = ==shared memory=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "// main.js",
                "const w = new Worker('./job.js', { workerData });",
                "w.on('message', handle);",
                "// job.js",
                "parentPort.postMessage(heavy(workerData));"
              ],
              "note": "workerData in, postMessage out"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Thread vs Process",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "worker_threads",
                "child_process",
                "cluster"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Unit",
                  "thread, same process",
                  "separate process + IPC",
                  "forked processes"
                ],
                [
                  "Weight",
                  "light",
                  "heavy",
                  "heavy"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "CPU-bound JS",
                  "other programs",
                  "requests on all cores"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pool, Not Per Task",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Use a ==pool== (e.g. `piscina`), not a worker per task",
                "{red:Spawn per request}: startup and memory cost every time",
                "{red:No workers for I/O}: async I/O is already non-blocking"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Which one?** Threads for CPU, cluster for cores, child_process for other programs",
                "**Sharing data?** Clone, transfer, or SharedArrayBuffer with Atomics",
                "**Worker per request?** Startup and memory cost; use a pool"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
